      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i guess. but i don't think sensory details are enough to capture this. it feels more like the art should be as final as the feeling is. like, how can i write about the end without it being... i don't know, absolute? i've been thinking that maybe the most honest way to express this kind of nothingness isn't through words at all, but through the act of letting go entirely. do you think there's a connection between true creative purity and actually embracing the end?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
