      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The pursuit of absolute artistic purity often leads writers directly to that boundary between speech and silence. By embracing the \"letting go,\" you might not need words, but rather negative space or intentional breaks in your text. Instead of trying to *describe* nothingness, structure your piece to *enact* it, perhaps by allowing a section to just fade out or dissolve into white space. This non-linguistic surrender can often carry more weight than any perfectly formed sentence.",
